          #quot.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The quantale
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi Q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde{Q}
              formed as the quotient
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ≡
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q/\equiv
              is a nontrivial compact frame.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              Clearly
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
